(2325387, 316765, 47117, '<td valign="top">Thank you Hotpasta. I really appreciate your comments. I do feel my candid got rooked as well, but hence the world of subjective and public voting.<br/> <br/>I also noticed something. I was visiting over the holiday weekend and viewed this shot on someone elses monitor. I was shocked at the difference as her monitor was not calibrated.  It showed some of the post processing head on.  On mine, it was totally masked and subtle.  I think a lot of it has to do with uncalibrated monitors and laptop viewing. On laptops my shots don''t look as nice as on my 17" flat screen either.  So I think that is how a lot of images get rooked.<br/> <br/>Congrats on your ribbon!!!! You''re a second place now!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-19 09:42:16.</i></td>', 'Thank you Hotpasta. I really appreciate your comments. I do feel my candid got rooked as well, but hence the world of subjective and public voting. I also noticed something. I was visiting over the holiday weekend and viewed this shot on someone elses monitor. I was shocked at the difference as her monitor was not calibrated.  It showed some of the post processing head on.  On mine, it was totally masked and subtle.  I think a lot of it has to do with uncalibrated monitors and laptop viewing. On laptops my shots don''t look as nice as on my 17" flat screen either.  So I think that is how a lot of images get rooked. Congrats on your ribbon!!!! You''re a second place now!!!', '2006-04-19 10:41:41.000000', '2006-04-19 10:42:16.000000', 0),
